# Cursor Rules for Airo AI Builder

## React Component Architecture

### Core Principles
- **Component-First Development**: Always build React pages using reusable components in their own files
- **No Hardcoded UI**: Never inline complex UI directly in pages - extract to dedicated components
- **Single Responsibility**: Each component should have one clear purpose
- **Consistent Structure**: Follow established patterns for component organization

### Component Organization
```
src/
├── app/
│   ├── [page]/
│   │   ├── page.tsx           # Page file - orchestrates components only
│   │   └── components/        # Page-specific components
│   │       ├── ComponentName.tsx
│   │       ├── types.ts       # Shared types for the page
│   │       └── index.ts       # Re-exports (optional)
│   └── components/            # Shared/global components
│       └── ui/                # Base UI components
```

### Page File Rules
- **Keep pages thin**: Pages should primarily import and orchestrate components
- **No inline JSX complexity**: If JSX is more than 5-10 lines, extract to a component
- **State management**: Keep page-level state minimal, push state down to components when possible
- **Import organization**: Group imports logically (React, Next.js, components, types)

### Component File Rules
- **One component per file**: Each `.tsx` file should export one main component
- **Clear naming**: Use PascalCase for components, match filename
- **Props interface**: Always define TypeScript interfaces for props
- **Export types**: Export interfaces that other components might need

### Example Patterns

#### ❌ Bad - Hardcoded UI in page
```tsx
export default function ChatPage() {
  return (
    <div className="flex">
      <div className="w-1/3 bg-white">
        <div className="p-4">
          <h2>Chat</h2>
          <div className="messages">
            {messages.map(msg => (
              <div key={msg.id} className="message">
                {msg.content}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <textarea />
          <button>Send</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div className="flex-1">
        {/* More inline UI... */}
      </div>
    </div>
  )
}
```

#### ✅ Good - Component-based architecture
```tsx
import ChatPane from './components/ChatPane'
import ContentPane from './components/ContentPane'

export default function ChatPage() {
  return (
    <div className="flex">
      <ChatPane 
        messages={messages}
        onSendMessage={handleSend}
      />
      <ContentPane />
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Refactoring Guidelines
- **Identify patterns**: Look for repeated UI patterns across pages
- **Extract components**: Move hardcoded UI to dedicated component files
- **Share interfaces**: Use common type definitions in `types.ts` files
- **Test incrementally**: Refactor one component at a time

### Component Composition
- **Prefer composition over inheritance**: Build complex UIs by combining simple components
- **Props drilling**: Avoid excessive prop drilling - consider context for deeply nested state
- **Component variants**: Use props to create variations rather than duplicate components

### Styling Guidelines
- **Consistent classes**: Use shared CSS classes and design tokens
- **Component-scoped styles**: Keep component-specific styles close to the component
- **Avoid inline styles**: Prefer Tailwind classes over inline styles (except for dynamic values)

### Performance Considerations
- **Lazy loading**: Use dynamic imports for large components
- **Memoization**: Use React.memo for expensive components
- **State optimization**: Keep state as local as possible

### Error Handling
- **Error boundaries**: Wrap component trees in error boundaries
- **Graceful degradation**: Components should handle missing props gracefully
- **Loading states**: Always handle loading and error states

## Enforcement
- Before creating any new page, first design the component structure
- When reviewing existing pages, always look for refactoring opportunities
- Prioritize component reusability and maintainability
- Document component APIs with clear prop interfaces

